WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:04.020
Members of the Praetorian Guard of the NOL

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:08.770
are all heroic men and women who've sworn allegiance to the Imperator.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.650
The convergence of their noble souls, which they've willingly offered,

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.570
is finally complete.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:20.540
We will now set this matter into motion.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:21.950
Having said that,

00:00:21.950 --> 00:00:25.670
hardly any time has passed since
Your Majesty's awakening.

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:29.460
For the time being, please conduct
your Imperial inspection from there.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:33.470
The Imperator and the Izayoi...

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.220
You've got to be losing your mind at all the things you can't see,

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.060
Takamagahara!

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:48.020
Terumi has his sights set on Noel Vermillion.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.610
She's always around when I don't want her to be, and just <i>now</i> she disappears!

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:02.040
Noel, this way.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:03.330
Where are we going?

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:06.120
First, I need to get in contact with Sector Seven.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.210
How?

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:08.500
Just follow me.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.960
I can sense him nearby.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.760
If I were him, what would I do?

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.880
He would definitely choose the shortest path!

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:56.530
Rebel 9: The Power of Order

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.700
<i>It was thin earlier and now it's thick here?</i>

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.320
<i>The concentration of seithr is unstable...</i>

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:08.870
I'm impressed you were able to track down this location, Litchi Faye-Ling.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:09.910
Who are you?!

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:15.540
The name's Hazama.
From the NOL Intelligence Department.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:16.750
Halt!

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.470
Oh, scary!

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:22.050
I'm not your enemy, just so you know.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:23.470
In fact,

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:26.560
I am a bringer of hope.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.680
What do you mean?

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.350
Take a look behind you.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:39.030
B-Body... Melting...

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.360
It can't be...

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.200
Oh, it <i>is</i> something that cannot be.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.830
This is the man that you hold dear.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:48.950
Roy!

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:52.370
Oh, Roy! Roy!

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.170
Litchi...

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:57.920
The fate of one who has plunged
into the depths of the Azure.

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:00.630
One who has fallen short of
becoming the Black Beast.

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:03.130
One messed up guy, ain't he?

00:04:03.130 --> 00:04:04.180
Shut up!

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:08.060
Now, what if I were to know
a way to take this ruined mess

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:11.390
and restore him to his former ol' self?

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.060
The NOL's guardhouse.

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:20.320
There aren't any Praetorian Guards here, either?

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:23.650
Not only that, but everyone from the Kagutsuchi Branch Office is also missing.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:25.030
But why?

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:27.530
I double checked with HQ,

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.240
but there weren't any large-scale evacuation scheduled.

00:04:30.620 --> 00:04:33.080
A whole host of Praetorian Guards has suddenly disappeared.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:37.920
Noel, I think I'll tell it to you straight after all.

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:39.090
What?

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.710
Knowing you, if I told you the truth,

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:46.090
I felt like you'd go running off
even if I tried to stop you.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.340
So I kept my mouth shut.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:48.970
What is it?

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.180
First, you have to promise me.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:55.810
Once you've heard what I'm about to say, you absolutely have to follow my orders.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.190
If you do, I'll tell you everything.

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:00.690
All right.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:05.950
When I left you earlier, I did a lot of digging around.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.490
The Kagutsuchi Branch Office was completely deserted.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:11.490
I found an odd altar at the top level.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:14.540
It was directly connected to the Cauldron right below it

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:18.250
and I sensed a really unpleasant aura emanating from it that wasn't seithr.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.960
A whole host of Praetorian Guards, gone...

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:24.920
It's likely to be the work of Captain Hazama.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:26.590
What do you mean?

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.140
The altar...

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:29.640
That unpleasant aura...

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.470
They're probably related in some way.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:36.140
All right. I think this should work.

00:05:36.850 --> 00:05:39.560
Comms are down, but this should reach her.

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:42.610
This is Gnu. Please come in.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:45.320
This is Gnu. Please come in.

00:05:49.030 --> 00:05:51.740
You're telling me that she's dreaming?

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:52.910
How?

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:55.370
Her memory should've been completely erased.

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:56.210
It's impossible.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:00.960
Does this mean that the soul itself has some form of memory retention?

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:04.630
The emergency channel?

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.090
Please...

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:08.380
Now what, Gnu?

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:12.140
Transmissions have been shit all week, so get to the point.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:14.720
I've found the lost child. Requesting for her to be evacuated.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:15.680
What?!

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:18.480
All right. I'll get someone to come pick you up.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:20.190
Rendezvous in 30 minutes.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:21.900
Do you read me, Tager?

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:24.690
I've been contacted by our collaborator.

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.650
She's seeking safe refuge for Noel Vermillion.

00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:28.610
What?

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:31.450
Head to the location I'm about to give you.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:36.290
Dr. Kokonoe is someone who's hard to read,

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:41.170
but at the very least, she's more trustworthy than Captain Hazama or the current NOL.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:46.760
She also said that you can't ever be allowed to come into contact with Captain Hazama.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:51.840
You said that you looked into Mr. Hazama's background, but that you couldn't find anything, right?

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:52.760
Yeah.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.850
There is absolutely no record of a "Captain Hazama" anywhere.

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:58.100
I don't even know who he is...

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:01.060
Yuuki Terumi...

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:03.730
How do you know that name?!

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:05.230
Oh, um...

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:06.940
I don't really get all of it, but...

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:09.110
I just like, saw it somewhere...

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.280
And Mr. Ragna also called him that.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:12.610
The Grim Reaper himself?!

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:16.410
Oh, honestly! There's just too much stuff that doesn't make any sense!

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:17.290
Dammit!

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:19.500
Where the hell is she?!

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.750
Argh! I'm sick of this crap already!

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:26.000
I ain't the kind of guy who protects people!

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:29.550
Okay, so I just have to go bash Terumi's skull in, right?

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:32.340
Makoto.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.300
What's up?

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:38.520
You mentioned earlier that there was
a reason you didn't tell me everything.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:43.980
This man named Hazama
supposedly doesn't exist.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:47.650
Yet, he currently holds unbelievable power.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:50.110
There is something wrong with the NOL right now.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:55.070
It's unthinkable that this man, who shouldn't exist,
is able to issue an Imperial Command to Tsubaki.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:56.910
What? So, you mean Tsubaki's...

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:00.290
In all likelihood, she's being used by Captain Hazama.

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:04.080
Tsubaki is most probably tracking down Major Kisaragi,

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.830
who is in turn pursuing the Grim Reaper.

00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:08.710
The Grim Reaper will head for the Kagutsuchi Branch Office where the Cauldron is located.

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:11.510
Everyone will gather in a single place.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:15.340
But, right now, the Kagutsuchi Branch Office is...

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.550
Tsubaki's in danger!

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.180
You can't! You promised, remember?!

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:23.230
Tsubaki will likely be okay.

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:25.440
If she hasn't be harmed so far,

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.860
it probably means that she's of
some use to Captain Hazama.

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:31.860
What are you saying?
And you call yourself her friend?!

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.280
I <i>am</i> her friend!

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:36.820
Both your and Tsubaki are my dearest and closest friends!

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:38.580
That's why...

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:43.580
It was fortunate that Tsubaki let you go.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:46.880
The worst thing would be for you to be caught by Captain Hazama.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.840
But even so...

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:51.760
Don't worry about Tsubaki.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:57.680
Once I've delivered you to safety, I'll absolutely go help her.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:08.520
Yukianesa...

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:10.690
It still won't activate.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:12.530
Brother Jin...

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:20.030
Tsubaki...

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:22.240
What are you doing here?

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:24.830
That uniform...

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:26.370
Yes.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:29.920
And I have a specific reason why
I appeared here dressed in this manner.

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:33.090
I trust you can figure out why.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.090
Major Jin Kisaragi,

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:42.760
you are currently charged with multible
instances of insubordination, and desertion.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:46.100
Lower your weapon at once and surrender yourself.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:49.190
I refuse.

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:52.900
Why?! If you would
just come quietly, then—

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:55.280
There is someone I must see.

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.570
I must meet this person
face to face and ascertain something.

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:00.490
Ascertain what?!

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:03.370
That is none of your business.

00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:08.330
You leave me no choice.

00:10:08.830 --> 00:10:09.830
In that case...

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:12.750
You'll use force?

00:10:12.750 --> 00:10:13.380
Yes.

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.710
You think you are capable of stopping me?

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:18.550
I know I am no match for you.

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:20.590
Which is why...

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:44.450
<i>A relic of the old war passed down in the Yayoi family since ancient times.</i>

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:46.790
<i>She even brought that to this fight...</i>

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:50.250
Why?! Why do you not draw your Nox Nyctores?!

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:54.750
<i>If Yukianesa will not activate, my offensive options are limited.</i>

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.960
Brother Jin!

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:01.260
Freeze!

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:08.060
It's no use!

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.520
The odds aren't looking in my favor...

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:16.980
Tager here. I've arrived at the rendezvous point.

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:18.780
Do you copy, Kokonoe?

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:23.120
Damn comms. There they go again.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.410
An direct consequence of the Sealed Armagus Izayoi.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:30.660
Looks like you arrived early for your lovely date,

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.790
Mr. Red "I'm from Sector Seven" Devil.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:38.260
So you're the infamous Yuuki Terumi.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:41.720
Oh, please. I'm only mild-mannered Hazama of the Intelligence Department right now.

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.090
But enough about me.

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:45.680
Since your date hasn't arrived, why don't the two of us have some fun in the meantime?

00:11:46.760 --> 00:11:48.890
Maybe I will ask you to keep me company, then.

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:50.770
Although...

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:52.890
...you may not enjoy it at all!

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:02.490
That armagus steals the light from its surroundings.

00:12:02.490 --> 00:12:04.200
Even that of its wielder.

00:12:04.610 --> 00:12:05.990
I am aware of it.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:07.330
Then why?!

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:09.330
Why would you still use it?!

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.870
To serve the will of the Imperator!

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:16.590
What is the Imperator to you?

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.800
The Imperator is the light! Absolute justice!

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:24.930
Condemning evil and bringing peace and order to this world, the Imperator is the people's hope!

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:29.970
Then I ask you: what of the people of Ikaruga, whose country was destroyed

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:32.430
all because they would not support the Imperator and the NOL?

00:12:32.810 --> 00:12:34.270
Were they guilty of any crime?

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:35.940
That's...

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:41.740
The one who brought an end to the Ikaruga Civil War was none other than yourself, Brother Jin!

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.240
I can hardly believe the Hero of Ikaruga would utter such words!

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:48.700
Even within the NOL, there were many who opposed the war.

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:54.460
But those have been purged in the name of the Imperator and at the hands of their own people.

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:58.040
By the Zero Squadron, whose ranks you have now joined.

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:01.460
The NOL. The Imperator.

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:05.340
Their hands carry the hammer of justice, but they are covered in blood.

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:08.090
This justice you speak of

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:10.220
is nothing but a dream!

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:11.720
Even so...

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:13.930
Even so, I...

00:13:13.930 --> 00:13:16.140
You are loyal, I'll give you that.

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:19.270
But the greater the thing you adhere to is,

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:21.980
the more you lose sight of what is around you.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:24.900
Stop trying to cast any more doubts on my beliefs!

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:29.910
Brother... Jin...

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:34.620
Tsubaki, do not be blinded by the mighty power that is the Imperator!

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:36.500
Power is necessary.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.840
Absolute power represents order!

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:43.050
Order...

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:45.970
The world is constantly strivin' for parity.

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:49.970
Should things tilt one way, a power to correct that tilt will also appear.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:51.470
And that's...

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:53.930
...the Power of Order...

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:01.690
Brother Jin?

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:03.440
I see.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:05.280
I understand now.

00:14:05.490 --> 00:14:06.990
It's thanks to you.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:08.660
What are you talking about?

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:13.410
Tsubaki, the order you speak of is the order found in mankind's world.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:16.660
It's but a small thing.

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:19.710
True order on the other hand...

00:14:27.760 --> 00:14:30.390
I never had any doubts to begin with.

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:33.720
I was merely refusing to accept my fate.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:35.970
Brother Jin...

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:38.270
I will show you, Tsubaki.

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:42.650
The order of the world. The power of balance.

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:45.070
I am Jin!

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:47.440
The blade that brings balance to the world!

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.610
Yukianesa, activate!

00:14:57.700 --> 00:15:01.540
This is Brother Jin's Nox Nyctores...

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:03.420
Yukianesa!

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:08.470
I feel as though I have woken from a long slumber.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:17.060
I never knew how powerful it really was...

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:19.430
Listen to me, Tsubaki.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:24.060
The Imperator is yet another force warping the natural way of the world.

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:26.650
Same as the Black Beast.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:30.320
Those words are perjury!

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:35.330
The light will be taken away from you.

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:37.790
Dismiss the armagus, Tsubaki.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:39.960
There will be no coming back otherwise.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:42.870
I care not!

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:43.420
However...

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:46.380
Charging ars magus! Disengage Restraint System!

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:52.180
<i>She's willing to die, sword in hand. Foolishness.</i>

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:53.510
Prepare yourself!

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:04.810
Do not presume, Tsubaki.

00:16:04.810 --> 00:16:07.900
Is that all your life is worth to you?

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:12.240
In your current state, you are not even worth killing.

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:25.210
Brother Jin...

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:26.130
Noel...

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:29.420
I have nothing now...

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:31.130
Nothing!

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:38.010
<i>This power...</i>

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:39.600
<i>I can feel it.</i>

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:41.930
<i>The purpose of my existence.</i>

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:46.270
<i>Thus far, I have been under Yukianesa's control.</i>

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:51.030
<i>But now, things will not be going your way anymore!</i>

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:53.190
<i>And at the same time,</i>

00:16:53.190 --> 00:16:56.660
<i>I now realize who my true enemy is:</i>

00:16:56.660 --> 00:16:59.580
<i>those who destroy the balance of this world.</i>

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:02.330
Brother.

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:08.840
You goin' in?

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:15.010
You're not gonna stop me, are you, Master?

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:18.180
Yer not one to stop just cuz someone told ya not to go.

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:21.850
You really <i>have</i> known me for a long time.

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:26.520
But Ragna, if yer goin', ya better remember what I'm about to tell ya.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:27.020
Huh?

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:29.610
Don't die.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:30.610
Okay?

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:34.940
I'm about to go kick some ass. You're gonna jinx me!

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.280
Even if ya can't win, just don't die.

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:38.620
Got that?

00:17:38.620 --> 00:17:40.280
Never give in to despair.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:43.290
Find a way to escape the jaws of death.

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:46.210
What's this? This ain't like you, Master.

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:48.880
Man, this is what getting old does to you.

00:17:48.880 --> 00:17:51.500
If ya end up dyin' in this fight,

00:17:51.500 --> 00:17:56.170
you'll only have been a man obsessed with revenge.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:59.840
But if ya <i>do</i> defeat him...

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:02.470
You're saying I'll be a hero or something?

00:18:02.470 --> 00:18:04.310
Hah! What a bunch of crap!

00:18:04.310 --> 00:18:06.940
I'm just here to kick his ass and smash the Cauldron.

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:08.480
That's it!

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:15.860
You do not intend to go to his aid, Master Jubei?

00:18:19.200 --> 00:18:24.620
In some sense, maybe it's us old-timers who are ghosts.

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:29.040
The ones who shape the new era must be the ones who live in the now.

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:30.670
Valkenhayn.

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:31.710
Milady.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.550
I'll be making a short stop before I return.

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:38.090
You return and prepare for tea.

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:40.260
Very well, milady.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:44.220
I shall have the very best financiers and tea waiting for you.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:48.140
I think it's about time I hit the road too.

00:18:48.140 --> 00:18:50.560
Give my best to Ragna.

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:51.440
I will not.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.230
You can give it to him yourself.

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:58.900
Oy vey, they've all got <i>something</i> wrong with them.

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:01.240
It should be around here.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:02.530
Who are we meeting—

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:03.200
Hey!

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:03.830
Hush!

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:10.750
This is the aftermath of a battle.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:13.710
I smell something burnt...

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:23.930
Captain Hazama!

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:32.270
Oh? I thought I smelled a wet dog. Turns out it was just a Beastkin.

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:33.650
Captain Hazama...

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:36.770
And you even brought your doll friend along!

00:19:36.770 --> 00:19:37.980
How lovely.

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:39.110
Doll?

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:40.570
Noel, stay back.

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:42.780
But too bad for you gals.

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:46.280
You arrived just as the show ended.

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:48.910
What's wrong, Tager?! Come in!

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:50.870
Run...

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.170
This is awful!

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:54.380
I won't let you lay a finger on Noel!

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:59.460
I guess that means you're up next, little mousy!

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:12.310
I...

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:15.190
For whom am I...

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:18.190
For what am I to live?

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:29.330
Brother Jin... Noel...

00:20:29.950 --> 00:20:30.950
I'm sorry.

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:32.370
I can no longer—

00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:39.630
Whence comest this doubt, Tsubaki Yayoi?

00:20:41.880 --> 00:20:45.050
Thou exist for mine sake.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:47.550
That is thine sole purpose.

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:50.390
It can't be... Impossible!

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:54.690
Tsubaki Yayoi, come join me by mine side.

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:58.980
Your Majesty!

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:02.690
I shall be the light to illuminate thee.

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:04.900
Dammit!

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.910
Why is nobody here?!

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:07.870
Is this a trap?

00:21:12.540 --> 00:21:13.960
A sudden chill...

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:22.590
We finally meet again, Brother.

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:26.800
Jin! You...

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:31.010
Now, shall we fight to our hearts' content?
